# The experiment log is written from three machines and merged without review, so it
# has to be mergeable by construction rather than by care.
#
# Per-machine shards, one self-describing JSON record per line, append-only. A union
# merge of two shards is then just concatenation of independent records, which is
# correct whatever schema either side was written under.
results/runs/*.jsonl merge=union

# Frozen history: every run recorded before the switch to shards. Nothing appends to
# this any more. Union stays on it only so a straggler commit from a machine that has
# not pulled yet still merges cleanly - and that is safe precisely because both sides
# now carry the same 57 columns.
#
# Do NOT put a migrating CSV behind a union driver again. Union merges LINES while a
# CSV's meaning lives in a header those lines share, so the moment two machines hold
# different column counts every row from one side is filed under the other's header.
# That produced 537 rows, 237 of them duplicates, seed 67 reading as 2 and run_dir
# holding a git SHA - from two inputs that were each individually clean.
results/runs.csv merge=union
